{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3308","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3308","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3308\",\"parent_revision\":\"d1ad361451f325c43b17c21bcf4fb27cd23c58632f4d66505384daf77f7d1442\",\"root_revision\":\"d1ad361451f325c43b17c21bcf4fb27cd23c58632f4d66505384daf77f7d1442\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nSurfaced by a Codex review comment on PR #3293, checked directly.\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` is a thin wrapper: its entire body is \\\"Invoke `/dh:work-backlog-item groom $ARGUMENTS` and follow its instructions.\\\" It does not reference any file under its own `references/` directory.\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` (and its siblings `issue-classification.md`, `groomer-output-validation.md`, `drift-check.md`) exist on disk but are not loaded by that `SKILL.md`, nor by any file under `work-backlog-item`'s own groom workflow (`groom/swarm.md`, `groom/analyze.md`, `groom/intake.md`, `groom/finalize.md` \u2014 all read directly this session, none reference `groom-backlog-item/references/`). The only repo-wide references to `groomer-agent.md` are in `docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` (a historical note), test fixtures, and auto-generated `graphify-out/*.json` \u2014 none of which execute it.\\n\\n`docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md:889-891` records a \\\"Session observation 2026-03-25\\\" stating these exact reference files did not exist on disk at that time (\\\"`groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` references `./references/issue-classification.md` and `./references/groomer-agent.md` \u2014 neither file exists on disk\\\"). They exist now, meaning something recreated them after that observation without restoring any load path from the current thin-wrapper `SKILL.md`.\\n\\nConcretely, `groomer-agent.md`'s two dispatch templates (lines 29-63, 70-99) still instruct pasting `item title`, `item description`, and every groomed-input section directly into a `dh:backlog-item-groomer` prompt \u2014 the exact anti-pattern #3268 fixed. If this file were ever wired back into an active load path without updating it, it would immediately reintroduce #3268's bug via a second, forgotten channel.\\n\\nUser-provided context: none \u2014 whether the fix is deleting these orphaned files, or restoring a genuine load path from `groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` and updating their dispatch templates to match the current `item_ref`-only contract, is a decision for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Codex review on PR #3293 (fix for #3268)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a35e38c13dbdfee8df72dbacfd1d769e69d33e598b1dbb3b376fcc33fe611ef0\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5b9w\"}"}